1.Write a program to check if a number is divisible by 5
I/P => number
O/P => Is the number ___ divisible by 5? ___
import java.util.Scanner;

public class DivisibleBy5 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter number: ");
        int num = sc.nextInt();

        if (num % 5 == 0) {
            System.out.println("Is the number divisible by 5? Yes");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Is the number divisible by 5? No");
        }
    }
}
Result
Enter number: 25
Is the number divisible by 5? Yes
Enter number: 23
Is the number divisible by 5? No

2. Write a program to check if the first is the smallest of the 3 numbers.
I/P => number1, number2, number3
O/P => Is the first number the smallest? ____
import java.util.Scanner;

public class SmallestCheck {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter 3 numbers: ");
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        int b = sc.nextInt();
        int c = sc.nextInt();

        if (a < b && a < c) {
            System.out.println("Is the first number the smallest? Yes");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Is the first number the smallest? No");
        }
    }
}
Result
Enter 3 numbers: 2 5 8
Is the first number the smallest? Yes
